@@ -2,48 +2,85 @@
 
 ## WebView rendering
 
-Platform change: `system/core` commit `3cd368f`,
-`libcutils: recognize sealed memfds when sandbox blocks readlink`.
+Platform change: system/core commit3cd368fe13898befe47a0b21bdd08a9d4ae12c51,
+libcutils: recognize sealed memfds when sandbox blocks readlink.
+WebView155 denied proc-fd readlink with EPERM, causing sealed memfds to be
+misclassified as ashmem. The fallback still requires grow/shrink seals and
+only accepts EPERM/EACCES. The original #55 tablet test covered that failure
+with ashmem present and restored HTML and JavaScript/Canvas rendering.
 
-On the tablet, WebView 155 failed to render because its sandbox denied
-`readlink(/proc/self/fd/N)` with EPERM. libcutils misclassified a sealed memfd
-as ashmem and aborted the renderer. The change permits the existing
-`F_GET_SEALS` check after EPERM/EACCES, retaining the mandatory grow/shrink
-seals. Other readlink errors still fail.
+The rebuilt62172-byte libcutils (SHA256
+4ebe48f84e2925cf9efad23c91039e1060e203558b5ca9f37f89a50f7678a462)
+was also tested on #54, then installed in the complete system image.
+After normal reboot, external HTTPS loaded and a local page reported60frames,
+correct Canvas pixel color and correct DOM layout. Screenshots confirmed
+rendered pages. Browser and renderer remained alive. A temporary DNS failure
+after zygote-only restart disappeared after the full reboot; do not treat it
+as evidence of an outstanding renderer failure.
 
-The corrected library was temporarily bind-mounted on the running tablet.
-After restarting zygote, HTML and a JavaScript/Canvas animation rendered
-successfully, with the renderer process remaining alive.
+## USB debugging across screen off and adbd restart
 
-The full system image subsequently built successfully. Its libcutils matches
-the build staging file; disassembly confirms the permission-error fallback
-and required seal checks. The signed recovery package passed CRC and image
-hash checks. The rebuilt image has not been installed or boot-tested.
+The recovered #55 log contained510 matching s2idle entry/exit pairs. The
+60-second health alarm aligned with physical USB reconnect cadence, narrowing
+the lost connection to repeated sleep/resume rather than a continuous hang.
+This does not prove every USB protocol error has the same cause.
 
-## Acoustic analysis utility
+The board usbwake service refreshes a ten-second kernel wake lock while the
+UDC has an active host state and a bound gadget. It releases for bus suspend,
+unplug and unbind. Checking the function is necessary: ChipIdea's state file
+remained configured after an observed unbind. The timeout bounds the lock
+if the service dies. Init starts the service on every boot.
+
+The serial fallback now waits for FunctionFS readiness before attempting g1.
+An init-owned test stopped adbd: g2 stayed bound at8seconds and16seconds.
+After restarting adbd, live reads confirmed adbd running and g1 bound.
+The original RTC service used to launch the test was restored afterward.
+A preliminary ADB-owned test had killed its own recovery worker when adbd
+stopped; that was a failed test, recovered through an actual root shell on
+the PVE physical USB serial console. PVE USB mapping was restored unchanged.
+
+Device checks:
 
-`tools/acoustic-check.py` analyzes an actual PCM16 WAV recording for the test
-sequence: 700 Hz, silence, 1100 Hz, silence, 1700 Hz, silence; one second per
-segment. It checks tone energy, separation from the following silence, and
-the proportion of signal power at each expected frequency.
+- Screen asleep, display bl_power4, Android stay-on disabled:13 successful
+  ADB samples over125seconds with only lt03lte_usb held, zero system suspends.
+- Final script:90seconds without ADB commands, screen asleep; connection
+  survived with zero system suspends.
+- After system installation and normal reboot, usbwake was running and held
+  lt03lte_usb before the diagnostic recovery lock was acquired.
+- Installed service: another90seconds idle with screen asleep, stay-on false,
+  only lt03lte_usb held; ADB survived and suspend count stayed0.
+- Connection and the same boot ID remained present at18:17, battery43%.
+- A killed temporary watcher released its lock after timeout.
+- Awake4KiB fsync and sync each completed in approximately0.06seconds.
 
-Checks performed:
+Physical unplug, host bus suspend and full system suspend/resume remain
+unverified. This preserves active USB debugging, and does not claim to fix
+GPU suspend recovery or F2FS latency across suspend.
 
-- Existing tablet recording: all samples zero; rejected.
-- Original generated stimulus: all three tones detected (analysis sanity check).
-- Synthetic delayed stimulus with noise: detected.
-- Synthetic continuous tones without the silence pattern: rejected.
-- Synthetic noise alone: rejected.
+## Installed image
 
-These checks validate the analysis utility, not tablet speaker or microphone
-operation. A new physical microphone recording must still pass after the
-codec fixes are tested.
+Full systemimage build passed. Signed recovery package CRC, EROFS integrity,
+raw-image SHA1 and extracted file hashes passed before installation.
+Package SHA256:64021f47ba6b9c3d58cdc579892d58948ecd70c26988aa4ab8d73f4e4ee689bb.
+Recovery installed the system; normal Android startup and changed boot ID
+confirmed the reboot. Installed libcutils, usbwake and usbswitch hashes match
+the verified image. Boot kernel remained #54; no pending codec kernel was
+flashed. Initial post-install dmesg had no WARNING, panic, BUG, checkpoint
+latency stack or system suspend entry. This is a bounded observation.
+
+## Acoustic analysis utility
 
-## Changes excluded from the tested set
+The tools/acoustic-check.py utility checks PCM16 WAV recordings for700Hz,
+silence,1100Hz,silence,1700Hz,silence, one second per segment. It checks tone
+energy, separation from silence and signal power at the expected frequency.
+The reference stimulus and delayed noisy synthetic recording passed.
+Continuous tones, noise alone and the actual all-zero tablet recording failed.
+These validate the utility, not physical speaker or microphone operation.
 
-The microphone/codec corrections only passed compilation. Speaker audibility,
-microphone input, sleep/resume stability, and VoLTE bidirectional call audio
-remain unverified. The tablet lost USB connectivity during a sleep/wake test;
-this does not establish whether the kernel hung or remained suspended.
+## Remaining hardware work
 
-No unverified kernel changes are included with this validation commit.
+Codec corrections passed compilation only. Actual speaker/microphone audio,
+full sleep/resume stability and VoLTE two-way call audio remain unverified.
+The old #55 log had one GPU devfreq warning and361 F2FS checkpoint latency
+stacks during repeated sleep; these require further diagnosis. No pending
+kernel or unverified VoLTE changes are included with this validation commit.
